From 6d731bc23bb439b5c1232b28c60285213da7f9b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:24:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AGS] Wire PCM playback end to end: decoder, source, device,
 RUNMANIFEST

Sound milestone S1 ("PCM on DOSBox-X"), the actual mechanism patch: uses
the mixer (dos_audio_mixer.h) and loader (dos_audio_decode.h) from the
previous two patches to replace the stubs patches 0016/0022/0023 left in
place for the COMPILES milestone. mojoAL/SDL2_sound stay gated out
(0005/0006) -- this never tries to make either work on DJGPP.

sdldecoder.cpp (DOS impl of SDLDecoder, kept SDLDecoder's real public
interface per 0022's own contract): Open() reads the whole clip into
memory (SDL_LoadFile_IO for a stream source; the existing in-memory
shared_ptr path for the other), calls dos_audio_decode_pcm(), and stores
the result as this decoder's own persistent buffer -- GetData() just
hands out non-owning slices of it (2048-sample/~186ms chunks) to the
existing, unchanged AudioPlayer::Poll()/OpenAlSource::PutData() chunked
pump. IsValid()/GetFormat()/GetChannels()/GetFreq()/GetPositionMs()/
GetDurationMs()/Seek()/EOS() all now reflect real state instead of the
"nothing decoded" stub answers; repeat wraps instead of ending at EOS,
matching the original SDL2_sound-backed behavior.

openalsource.cpp (DOS impl of OpenAlSource, same kept-interface
contract): acquires one dos_audio_mixer voice per instance (released in
a new, no-longer-defaulted destructor), forwards PutData/volume/Play/
Pause/Stop to it. SetPanning stays a no-op (the mixer bus is mono) and
SetSpeed stays tracked-but-unapplied (no real-time resampling in S1) --
both pre-existing stub behaviors, not regressions. GetPositionMs() keeps
the existing _predictTs running-estimate approach.

sys_main.cpp: sys_audio_init() now actually calls
SDL_InitSubSystem(SDL_INIT_AUDIO) + dos_audio_mixer_init() instead of
unconditionally returning false; sys_audio_shutdown() closes the mixer's
stream before quitting the subsystem underneath it. Caught and fixed a
real SDL3 API-migration bug while wiring this up: SDL_InitSubSystem()
returns bool in SDL3 (true = success), not SDL2's "0 = success" int --
the first version of this check inverted the result and silently treated
a successful init as a failure (confirmed by a DOSBox-X run: "Failed to
init SDL audio subsystem: " with an empty SDL_GetError(), i.e. no actual
error had occurred).

audio_core.cpp: audio_core_entry_poll()'s existing per-slot AudioPlayer
poll loop (already reached by WaitForNextFrame() on every normal frame)
gains one dos_audio_mixer_pump() call after that loop -- the single
choke point that mixes active voices into the shared stream and services
the SB ring.

game_run.cpp: UpdateGameOnce's play.fast_forward/skip_render_and_wait
early return (added by patch 0047, S0) skips WaitForNextFrame() and
therefore its own audio_core_entry_poll() call -- added a second,
narrowly-scoped pump call in that branch so a fast-forwarded cutscene or
a fixed-timestep catch-up run still gets audio serviced. Deliberately
NOT added to the shared update_polled_stuff() a few lines above instead
(the plan's own wording, "the fast-forward path needs the pump too",
reads as if that were the natural hook): update_polled_stuff() has 17
OTHER call sites across screen fades, dialog options, GUI buttons, and
room loading -- tight per-step polling loops, not per-tick ones -- and
routing a full mixdown through all of them measured as a real ~35%
duration regression on this same harness (RUNMANIFEST duration_s 110 ->
160, fps_p50 34.6 -> 23.8) before being caught and reverted in favor of
this narrower placement, which reproduces the original baseline exactly.

quit.cpp: manifest.audio_vital_status is now set from
dos_audio_mixer_status_string() before runmanifest_emit(). That function
reads live state, but shutdown_sound() (called earlier in quit(), see
audio.cpp) has ALREADY torn the device down via sys_audio_shutdown() by
the time this runs -- so dos_audio_mixer_shutdown() (previous patch's
own file) snapshots the status string into a static buffer right before
tearing the stream down, and the getter falls back to that snapshot once
the live stream is gone. Without this, RUNMANIFEST would report NA even
after every clip loaded and played correctly, since the manifest is only
built once, at final clean shutdown, well after the device closes.

Verified on DOSBox-X, tests/harness (agsquest): all 18 phases + optional
dialog ok, all 3 screenshots byte-identical to the existing baseline,
RUNMANIFEST audio_vital_status=pcm=sb@11025m16,voices=8,underruns=0;
midi=none (the "no MIDI backend yet" placeholder S4 replaces once a real
one exists) -- this port's own overlay WAV chime (autopilot_chime.wav)
now actually loads and plays (no more "unable to load sound file" for
that clip); the MIDI tune and the game's own pre-existing OGG clips
still fail the same way they always have, expected since neither has a
decoder in S1's scope. Confirmed both with SDL_HINT_DOS_SILENCE_DETECT
at its default and forced to 0 (already-vendored SDL patches 0056/0057,
no engine-side wiring needed) -- identical results either way. Confirmed
together with DOSAGS_FIXED_TIMESTEP=1 (S0): frames_skipped=193 (catch-up
ticks fired), audio_vital_status still clean, all phases still ok.
